# db-per-company T6 (model D-8/D-33): seals a tenant's generated password
# (credentialRef `enc:v1`) the same way node-files' NF_SECRET_KEY seals a
# workflow credential — AES-256-GCM, 32 bytes, hex (64 chars) or base64.
# Deliberately its own variable, not a reuse of NF_SECRET_KEY: a leak of one
# key must not also expose the other's secrets.
TENANT_CREDENTIAL_KEY=

# Optional recipient allowlist for module/account email (Resend). Comma list;
# "@domain.com" matches a whole domain, anything else an exact address,
# case-insensitive. Unset or empty = send to everyone. Set it on dev so test
# data can never mail real customers.
# EMAIL_ALLOWED_RECIPIENTS=@genium.io,me@example.com

# Password for the provisioning admin identity referenced by
# db_servers.adminCredentialRef ('env:SQL_ADMIN_PASSWORD'). Provisioning runs
# CREATE ROLE / CREATE DATABASE .. OWNER / ALTER DATABASE .. SET mobius.*, and
# that last one needs SUPERUSER for a customized two-part parameter — so this is
# the password of a privileged provisioning role, never the app's own role.
# Locally the cluster trust-authenticates over TCP and ignores the value, but it
# must be non-empty: resolveCredential() rejects an empty env credential.
SQL_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
